 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "theres water in the bottom of my frige under the salad draws, keeps comming back after i mop it up"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That recurring water is most often caused by a blocked defrost drain at the back of the fridge, though it could also be excess condensation from warm food or a slightly off-level unit. To check this safely, please switch the appliance off and unplug it first to avoid any electrical risk. Then look for the small drain hole at the bottom of the rear wall inside the fridge compartment; if you see debris there, gently clear it with warm water using a turkey baster or soft pipe cleaner. Let me know if that hole was blocked and whether clearing it stops the water from returning after an hour."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok i unpluged it and had a look, theres a little groove at the bottom of the back wall with a hole and it was full of bits of lettuce and gunk. i cleared it with a cotton bud and warm water and the water went straight down. no more puddle for the last few days so far. the water was only ever inside the fridge, nowhere near the plug. is there anything else i should do to stop it happening again?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That is excellent news! Since the drain was blocked with debris and you have cleared it successfully, that was almost certainly the cause of your water issue. To help stop this happening again, try to avoid placing food items directly against the back wall so they don't trap gunk in the drain channel. Please keep an eye on it for a day or two to ensure it stays dry, and let me know if there is anything else I can assist you with today."
  }
 ],
